==============================================================================
THREAD A synthesis: the modular structure of the LRC residue discrepancy
==============================================================================

LAW:  S_P(p,q) = [2 A B (P-A)(P-B) + 2 C (P-C)]/P, A=||p||,B=||q||,C=||pq||.

Klein-4 orbit decomposition of P^1(F_P) and S-value per orbit (= the dessin cells):

  P=5:  #slopes=6, #Klein-4 orbits=3  (predicted (P+3)/4 *2-ish)
     orbit size  2: [0, 'inf']  -> S-values [0] APEX(S=0)
     orbit size  2: [1, 4]  -> S-values [8] 
     orbit size  2: [2, 3]  -> S-values [12] 

  P=7:  #slopes=8, #Klein-4 orbits=3  (predicted (P+3)/4 *2-ish)
     orbit size  2: [0, 'inf']  -> S-values [0] APEX(S=0)
     orbit size  2: [1, 6]  -> S-values [12] 
     orbit size  4: [2, 3, 4, 5]  -> S-values [20, 24] 

  P=11:  #slopes=12, #Klein-4 orbits=4  (predicted (P+3)/4 *2-ish)
     orbit size  2: [0, 'inf']  -> S-values [0] APEX(S=0)
     orbit size  2: [1, 10]  -> S-values [20] 
     orbit size  4: [2, 5, 6, 9]  -> S-values [36, 60] 
     orbit size  4: [3, 4, 7, 8]  -> S-values [48, 56] 

  P=13:  #slopes=14, #Klein-4 orbits=5  (predicted (P+3)/4 *2-ish)
     orbit size  2: [0, 'inf']  -> S-values [0] APEX(S=0)
     orbit size  2: [1, 12]  -> S-values [24] 
     orbit size  2: [5, 8]  -> S-values [80] 
     orbit size  4: [10, 3, 4, 9]  -> S-values [60, 72] 
     orbit size  4: [11, 2, 6, 7]  -> S-values [44, 84] 

  # non-apex Klein-4 orbits (the 'inner cells' of the dessin):
     P= 5: total orbits 3, non-apex 2  (orbit sizes [2, 2, 2])
     P= 7: total orbits 3, non-apex 2  (orbit sizes [2, 2, 4])
     P=11: total orbits 4, non-apex 3  (orbit sizes [2, 2, 4, 4])
     P=13: total orbits 5, non-apex 4  (orbit sizes [2, 2, 2, 4, 4])
     P=17: total orbits 6, non-apex 5  (orbit sizes [2, 2, 2, 4, 4, 4])
     P=19: total orbits 6, non-apex 5  (orbit sizes [2, 2, 4, 4, 4, 4])
     P=23: total orbits 7, non-apex 6  (orbit sizes [2, 2, 4, 4, 4, 4, 4])

LRC-type sharp face for general P (window 1<p/q<P, in-window coprime ratios):
  sup over the window of S_P/(P q) [= D*p side] and S_P/(P p) need the SPECIFIC
  small-denominator ratios; we report the dominant residue cell maxima:
   P= 5: max S_P=16; S_P(3,2)=16  (P=7: this is the 36 giving 12/7 face)
   P= 7: max S_P=44; S_P(3,2)=36  (P=7: this is the 36 giving 12/7 face)
   P=11: max S_P=168; S_P(3,2)=84  (P=7: this is the 36 giving 12/7 face)
   P=13: max S_P=276; S_P(3,2)=108  (P=7: this is the 36 giving 12/7 face)

=> CLEANEST MODULAR CHARACTERIZATION:
   S_P is a sum of two CYCLE-GRAPH GREEN'S FUNCTIONS (= weight-2 Bernoulli/Eisenstein
   B_2 values) of the P-cycle, in the variables (||p||,||q||) and (||pq||); it is a
   class function on P^1(F_P)/<+-,inversion> (Klein-4, ALL P>=5), the +- hyperelliptic
   x modular-inversion quotient.  For P=7 the ambient P^1(F_7)/PSL(2,7) is the Klein
   quartic X(7); the Klein-4 quotient has 3 cells {apex 0/inf, edge, bulk} = a dessin
   over {0,1,inf}.  The order-3 (doubling/QR/cubic) structure of X(7) does NOT act on
   S_P -- only the order-2 part survives, exactly as HYP-2742 found, now for all P.
